# | Symbol             | Name / Type               | Meaning & Use Case                      | Example                   |
# | ------------------ | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
# | `=`                | Assignment Operator       | Assigns a value to a variable           | `x = 5`                   |
# | `==`               | Equality Operator         | Checks if two values are equal          | `x == 5`                  |
# | `!=`               | Not Equal                 | Checks if values are not equal          | `x != y`                  |
# | `<, >`             | Comparison Operators      | Less than / Greater than                | `x < 10`                  |
# | `<=`               | Less than or equal to     | Comparison                              | `x <= 5`                  |
# | `>=`               | Greater than or equal     | Comparison                              | `x >= 5`                  |
# | `+`                | Addition or Concatenation | Add numbers or strings                  | `3 + 4`, `"a" + "b"`      |
# | `-`                | Subtraction               | Subtract numbers                        | `10 - 5`                  |
# | `*`                | Multiplication            | Multiply numbers                        | `2 * 3`                   |
# | `/`                | Division                  | Divides numbers (returns float)         | `10 / 3` → `3.33`         |
# | `//`               | Floor Division            | Returns whole number only               | `10 // 3` → `3`           |
# | `%`                | Modulo                    | Remainder of division                   | `10 % 3` → `1`            |
# | `**`               | Exponentiation            | Power of a number                       | `2 ** 3` → `8`            |
# | `:`                | Colon                     | Used in dicts, loops, function blocks   | `if x:`, `"key": "value"` |
# | `[]`               | Brackets                  | Used for lists, arrays, indexing        | `my_list[0]`              |
# | `{}`               | Braces                    | Define dictionary or set                | `{"a": 1}`, `set()`       |
# | `()`               | Parentheses               | Grouping, function calls                | `print()`, `(a + b)`      |
# | `->`               | Function return hint      | Type hinting in functions               | `def func() -> int:`      |
# | `,`                | Comma                     | Separates items                         | `a, b = 1, 2`             |
# | `.`                | Dot                       | Access object properties/methods        | `obj.method()`            |
# | `in`               | Membership test           | Checks if value exists in a collection  | `if 3 in [1, 2, 3]`       |
# | `not`, `and`, `or` | Logical operators         | Combine conditions                      | `if a and b:`             |
# | `is`               | Identity comparison       | Checks if two variables are same object | `a is b`                  |
# | `#`                | Comment                   | Adds a comment                          | `# This is a comment`     |
# | `"""`              | Docstring / multi-line    | Multi-line string or documentation      | `"""Hello"""`             |
